    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d479">

                <pb facs="0901" n="873" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v15/pg873"/>

                <head>479. Memorandum of a Telephone Conversation Between the Secretary of State and
                    the Director of Central Intelligence (Dulles), Washington, July 19, 1956, 5:30
                        p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d479-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            type="conversation-or-meeting-date" when="1956-07-19T17:30:00-04:00"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">July 19, 1956, 5:30
                    p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>The Sec. called and said he had just finished his talk with the Egyptian
                        Amb.,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d479-f2"/> who had handled himself surprisingly
                    well and with dignity. The Secretary read AWD the statement and the latter
                    thought it was a good one.</p>
                <p>The Sec. gave a précis of what he had told Hussein.</p>
                <pb facs="0902" n="874" xml:id="pg874"/>
                <p>AWD said he would like some copies of the press release on the Aswan Dam as soon
                    as he could have them so he could have it for his purposes, (cjp<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d479-f3"/> is handling)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
